051 - Day Is Dying in the West
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 51
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[G]Day is dying [C/G]in the west; [G]Heaven is touching earth with [C/G]rest;
[C/G]Wait and [G]worship while [D7]the night [G/D]Sets her evening lamps [D]alight
[D7/F#]Through all [G]the [A7]sky.
[A#dim]Holy, [Bm]holy, [G]holy, [D/A]Lord God [Am]of hosts! [D]Heaven [G]and earth are full of Thee;
[G]Heaven and earth are praising [D7]Thee, O Lord most [G]high!

Refrain:
[C]Holy, [D7/C]holy, [C]holy, Lord God [G]of Hosts!
[G]Heaven and [D7]earth are full of [G]Thee!
[G]Heaven and [C]earth [G/D]are praising Thee,
[G]O Lord most high!

Verse 2:
[G]Lord of [C/G]life, [G]beneath the dome
[C/G]Of [G]the universe, [D7]Thy [D]home,
[D7/F#]Gather us [G]who seek [A7]Thy [Am]face
[A#dim]To [Bm]the [G]fold [D/A]of Thy [G]embrace,
[G]For Thou art [D7]nigh.

Verse 3:
[G]While [C/G]the deepening [G]shadows fall,
[C/G]Heart [G]of love [D7]enfolding [D]all,
[D7/F#]Through the glory [G]and [A7]the [Am]grace
[A#dim]Of [Bm]the [G]stars [D/A]that veil [G]Thy face,
[G]Our hearts ascend.

Verse 4:
[G]When forever from our sight
[C/G]Pass [G]the stars, [D7]the [G/D]day, [D7]the [D]night,
[D7/F#]Lord of angels, [G]on [A7]our [Am]eyes
[A#dim]Let [Bm]eternal [D]morning [G]rise
[G]And shadows [D7]end.
